Z||000000||MooCow||06-25-2001||10:33 AM||||Geez everytime I put a fuse in it blows with in a day or so.  The fuse I keep using is the correct size fuse.  Also it is the one so I have dome lights and power locks and power trunk release.  Anyone know why it keeps blowing??<P>                               Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||8
Z||000001||84Bill||06-25-2001||11:42 AM||||I think you may have an intermitant short somewhere  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>Seriously what does the fuse power, it's hard to track down the problem if the circut is not known. A few more details would help us determin what the problem might be.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000002||PBJ||06-25-2001||01:13 PM||||here is what I would do.  get a spare working headlight and wire up about three feet of wire to it and connecter on the end that fit into fuse contacts.  remove fuse and put the headlight in its place-sooo the headlight is now the fuse.  when it lights up with FULL brightness the short is present.<BR>Sooo drive your vehicle and see what you do to get the light to come on bright-to make the short to happen.  could try accessories that are on the circuit and pull on/move wires around.<P>Intermitent shorts take time to find.||||reg||1
